==============================================================================
F2. Analytic proof R(z) <= 1/z for z>0 (own re-derivation)
==============================================================================
R(z) = e^{z^2/2} int_z^inf e^{-t^2/2} dt.
For t>=z>0: t/z >= 1, so e^{-t^2/2} <= (t/z) e^{-t^2/2}.
Integrate: int_z^inf e^{-t^2/2}dt <= (1/z) int_z^inf t e^{-t^2/2}dt = (1/z) e^{-z^2/2}
 [since d/dt(-e^{-t^2/2}) = t e^{-t^2/2}, so int_z^inf t e^{-t^2/2}dt = e^{-z^2/2}]
Hence R(z) = e^{z^2/2}*int_z^inf e^{-t^2/2}dt <= e^{z^2/2}*e^{-z^2/2}/z = 1/z.  QED, matches target's/lineage's cited fact.
sympy check d/dt(-e^{-t^2/2}) - t*e^{-t^2/2} = 0  -> PASS

